input.content:
DataQ {{ .Chart.AppVersion }} is installed as {{ include "dataq.fullname" . }} in {{ .Release.Namespace }}.

The frontend is the only way in; the api has no external address.
{{- if .Values.ingress.enabled }}
  {{ include "dataq.publicBaseUrl" . }}
{{- else }}
  kubectl -n {{ .Release.Namespace }} port-forward svc/{{ include "dataq.fullname" . }}-frontend 8080:{{ .Values.frontend.service.port }}
  then open http://localhost:8080
{{- end }}

Check it: GET /healthz through the frontend returns 200, you can sign in, and one suite run
completes.

